# TypeScript Type Definitions

## Core Types

### ParsedReceipt
```typescript
interface ParsedReceipt {
  store: string
  date: Date
  items: ParsedReceiptItem[]
  total: number
}

interface ParsedReceiptItem {
  name_raw: string
  price: number
  quantity: number
}
```

### Database Types (Supabase)

```typescript
// Users
interface User {
  id: string
  email: string
  created_at: string
}

// Receipts
interface Receipt {
  id: string
  user_id: string
  store_name: string
  store_chain: string
  purchase_date: string
  total_amount: number
  receipt_image_url: string
  created_at: string
}

// Receipt Items
interface ReceiptItem {
  id: string
  receipt_id: string
  product_name_raw: string
  normalized_product_id: string | null
  price: number
  quantity: number
  unit_price: number
  created_at: string
}

// Products
interface Product {
  id: string
  name: string
  category: string
}

// Price Observations
interface PriceObservation {
  id: string
  product_id: string
  store_chain: string
  store_name: string
  price: number
  timestamp: string
  receipt_id: string
}

// Shopping Lists
interface ShoppingList {
  id: string
  user_id: string
  name: string
  created_at: string
}

interface ShoppingListItem {
  id: string
  list_id: string
  product_id: string
  quantity: number
}
```

### Service Types

```typescript
// Price Optimizer Result
interface PriceComparisonResult {
  option1: {
    stores: string[]
    total: number
  }
  option2: {
    stores: string[]
    total: number
  }
}

// Analytics Types
interface MonthlySpending {
  month: string
  total: number
}

interface StoreSpending {
  store_chain: string
  total: number
}
```

## Type Location

All types should be defined in `/types` directory:
- `types/receipt.ts` - Receipt-related types
- `types/product.ts` - Product-related types
- `types/shopping.ts` - Shopping list types
- `types/analytics.ts` - Analytics types
- `types/index.ts` - Re-export all types

## Type Safety Rules

- **Never use `any`**: Use `unknown` if type is truly unknown
- **Use interfaces**: Prefer interfaces over type aliases for object shapes
- **Strict null checks**: Handle nullable fields explicitly
- **Generic types**: Use generics for reusable components/services
